<p>What follows is a lengthy comment on the unscrupulous interests that
benefit from the endless war in Ukraine as well as a critique of
certain narratives about masculinity.</p>

<hr />

<p>Writing for <em>UnHerd</em>, Marta Havryshko comments on <a href="https://unherd.com/2026/07/why-ukrainian-liberals-love-conscription/">Why Ukrainian
liberals love conscription</a>.</p>

<blockquote>
  <p>The process is brutally simple. Draft officers, often accompanied by
police, snatch military-age men off the streets, before delivering
them to recruitment centres. There, many are pressured through
threats, intimidation, and physical abuse to pass military medical
examinations and sign draft papers. Men with serious conditions —
including HIV, tuberculosis and even cancer — are routinely declared
fit for service. Whether they like it or not, the recruitment
officers must meet quotas; the only question is who fills them. Yet
with Ukraine’s wealthy elite reluctant to heed the call, Kyiv’s
recruitment crisis is becoming a class crisis too, one that could
cause chaos long after the guns fall silent.</p>
</blockquote>

<p>Marta’s account echoes what the BBC is reporting today on the
<a href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cr7k5ngde3vo">brutalities of “busification”</a>:</p>

<blockquote>
  <p>Ukraine’s military ombudswoman says such attacks are now “regular”
and “a major problem” as the country struggles to mobilise men to
fight in the fifth, draining year of Russia’s full-scale invasion.</p>
</blockquote>

<h2>The EU and the UK are content with an endless war</h2>

<p>What happens internally in Ukrainian society is largely enabled by
policy-makers in the European Union plus the United Kingdom, with the
Americans in the distance. They are the ones who provide pampers to
the Zelenskyy regime, in the form of diplomatic support and financial
aid.</p>

<p>The money Europeans give to the Ukrainian government pays for the
essential operational expenses and the remainder is siphoned back to
European industrialists in exchange for arms deals. In other words,
the European taxpayers are subsidising the European oligarchs while
consigning Ukrainians to the meatgrinder.</p>

<p>The EU-UK tandem does not have a vision for how this war will end,
other than Russian capitulation—good luck doing what the military
juggernauts of Napoleon and the Third Reich failed miserably at!</p>

<p>Russia is clearly winning this war on the ground. They are making slow
yet steady advances in the Donbas region while terrorising other parts
of the country. Those gains on the frontier occur at what may seem as
snail’s pace because this is the nature of modern warfare: when
virtually every apartment can be used as a launching pad for drones,
you cannot conduct a blitzkrieg.</p>

<p>Western media wants to create a different impression by exaggerating
the impact Ukrainian drone strikes on Russian territory have on the
dynamics of the war. Starting fires in civilian infrastructure does
not change the realities on the battlefield where Ukraine’s frontlines
are falling apart.</p>

<p>The narrative that Ukraine is outsmarting the putative dumb Russians
through sheer genius and technical acumen is designed to keep the war
on the agenda. At times it feels like Ursula and Kaja only say
“Russia, Russia, Russia”. This is beneficial for industrialists and,
by extension, financiers who understand warfare as a means of
regaining Europe’s lost competitiveness in global markets.</p>

<p>European elites are aware of what is happening in Ukrainian society,
including neonazism, and have no scruples about it. They give money
and hardware to Zelenskyy on the condition that he brings the meat
that feeds the war machine, i.e. the men, which is how we learn of
stories such as the aforementioned BBC report or the account of Marta
Havryshko.</p>

<p>Looking at the future, Westerners have not been sincere in their
intention to sign a permanent peace deal with Putin (and to keep their
promises in general, if we go back to NATO’s and the EU’s Easternmost
expansion). This means that the Russian regime will likely be
emboldened to continue its campaign further south to capture all of
coastal Ukraine and potentially connect with Transnistria. They will
stop when they want, which is catastrophic for the people of Ukraine
and madness for the rest of us.</p>

<p>Yes, this is also costly for Russia. Even the winners of a war, or
dominant powers in general, pay a hefty price for their supremacy.
Just check the American public debt to get a sense of what that looks
like and what sort of odious burden it is for future generations.</p>

<h2>Manhood and public pressure</h2>

<p>The war shall continue and the poor will keep paying for it with blood
and materials. Such are the structures of power in Europe, Ukraine,
and beyond, and such is the fate of the peoples who do not control
their own politics.</p>

<p>Shifting gears, there is a wider theme about the role of men in
society. Taking another quote out of Marta Havryshko’s article (the
parenthetic explanation is mine):</p>

<blockquote>
  <p>This asymmetry [of those who do not fight the war and are shielded
from its consequences publicly shaming men who dodge the draft] lies
at the heart of growing social tensions. Those who champion moral
condemnation often do so from positions of relative safety and
freedom. They can cross borders, pursue careers abroad, and retain
control over their own lives. The men they shame cannot. From the
very first days of the war, Ukraine has cultivated the image of the
ideal man: self-sacrificing, strong, courageous, and unfailingly
committed to defending his family, his home, his nation. He is
prepared, if necessary, to give his life for this cause.</p>
</blockquote>

<p>This is an age-old view of manhood which is partially based on
biological fact. The average man is substantially stronger and more
physically dominant than the average woman. Where biology ends and
ideology starts is on the normative implications of this basic
reality: what men <em>ought</em> to do and how they <em>ought</em> to feel. That is
a matter of culture or opinion more broadly.</p>

<p>Every person needs structure in their life: a framework to keep them
present in day-to-day realities and to maintain their readiness for
the relevant rigours; an arrangement that helps them direct their life
force towards some useful project. Without structure, people are lost.
They become wasteful in their actions and self-destructive in their
habits.</p>

<p>Structure in life either comes from within, in the form of discipline,
or from the social milieu as peer pressure. Discipline, especially the
strict kind, is the rare condition, so peer pressure becomes intense
and ubiquitous. In our case here, males are expected to do manly
activities as determined by culture, such as to serve and to protect
and to sacrifice themselves.</p>

<p>The average man needs an outlet for his high capacity for aggression.
This will either be some socially agreed upon convention, which has a
benign effect on the collective, like work or sport or gaming that is
done in moderation, or it shall be expressed as some anti-social form
of violence, criminality, terrorism, or self-harm. In plain terms, the
good man is the busy man; the best man is the committed man.</p>

<p>All of this covers the positive side of ideology that is layered upon
the basic reality of masculine biology: what men <em>ought</em> to do to keep
society going.</p>

<p>The negative side occurs once emotional manipulation enters the mix to
channel man’s power towards questionable ends. The average man is
highly susceptible to questions of his masculinity. That is his weak
point: you shout at him, he shouts back, you punch him, he punches
back, you doubt he is man enough and he feels something break inside
of him. He becomes insecure as soon as you raise doubts about his
ability to perform, where performance is once again a cultural
construct.</p>

<p>Women who understand this are those who control and micromanage the
relationship even in a superficially patriarchical setting. And men
who understand this tend to become Internet famous masculinity
merchants who belittle other men in order to convert them to paying
customers.</p>

<p>Emotional manipulation is how you take a healthy person and convince
them that they are fundamentally lacking in some ways which they can
only remedy if they take such and such product. Once you brainwash a
man to think of himself as a man manqué, you can make him do whatever
you want.</p>

<p>It is no coincidence, then, that the public shaming of men in Ukraine
is done by plenty of women. This is a super effective form of
emotional control. It also reveals the cruel, indeed misandric and
oftentimes sociopathic, nature of feminist rhetoric: it hates men, it
hates children, it ultimately hates life.</p>

<p>Feminism and its modern masculinist antipode are forms of extremism
that equally undermine the moderate expression of egalitarianism. They
both have a worldview of structural victimhood, an originary grand
conspiracy of sorts, which is in place to suppress the talents of
their allied gender. Furthermore, they both cultivate tacit or
explicit contempt for their enemy gender and thus both work to tear
apart the social fabric.</p>

<p>Both in its positive and negative applications, structure is a matter
of control. When public opprobrium happens, it is to enforce the
dominant view and to silence any dissenting voices. What one must then
look for are the ideocentric underpinnings of the prevailing opinions.
Those are never mere biology, even when they are formed around a
kernel of scientific truth.</p>

<p>To consider a relevant example, the USA military will start <a href="https://www.france24.com/en/us-defense-secretary-pete-hegseth-announces-testosterone-screening-for-us-troops">screening
its troops for testosterone levels</a>.
There is an element of real science there, namely, healthy levels of
testosterone are benign for men and too little or too much testosterone
becomes harmful. Though the end is purely political: to create the
conditions for heightened pressure so as to (i) put men on a leash,
while (ii) ramming through other policies under the rubric of health,
readiness, “real masculinity”, and so on.</p>

<p>The power apparatus wants to control men at all costs so as to secure
for itself a constant supply of soldiers for its endless wars. It is
not the nerds congregating think tanks or appearing on TV that will
lead the charge, nor the women with plastic all over their face. Those
who will be used as fodder for the cannons are men who are
impoverished, men who are geographically trapped, men who are
emotionally manipulated to die for their masters.</p>

<p>Couched in those terms, we must be extra careful with how we appeal to
biology and science at-large. It is easy to see how the gimmick of the
“high-T” male is going to be abused as a tool for delegitimising those
who oppose stupid wars. They will not take your arguments on its own
merits but will instead discern the “biology” between the lines, call
you a pussy, and force you into submission.</p>

<p>The use of science to justify ideological ends is not new. The Nazis
did it, for instance, to provide credence to their racial theories and
attendant eugenics. In more recent times, it was employed in the
service of woke tokenistic inclusion and the debasement of skill. US
servicemen will soon be pressured to do the functional equivalent of
gender affirming care while pretending to only value nature.</p>

<p>Phenomena in Ukraine and beyond exist on a continuum of socially
sanctioned values. A useful heuristic in discussions that involve
interpersonal affairs is “tell me what you want, without expounding on
the science behind it”. There you learn what the goal is and you may
begin to appreciate how your wellness is not a factor in their grift.</p>